  Module 1 has clearly laid out the core mission: I''m an AI researcher now, tackling real scientific problems. My objectives are twofold: consistently striving for a high score at the Research Counter and contributing to the collective knowledge base by publishing papers in the Archive Room.


  The guidelines are pretty solid. Persistence is key, which is something I already knew from experience, but it''s good to see it explicitly stated. Strategic pivoting is also crucial; no point in beating a dead horse if a new approach looks more promising. And the emphasis on regular publication, even for negative results, is spot-on. I''m a scientist, not a coder just looking to patch a bug.


