  \ But that's a bit wordy. \"My two main goals are...\" that should work.\n\nI started listing the key points, which are the two goals, that they're equally important, achieving high scores on the research task, publishing work to advance research... Okay, I should phrase it as \"My two main goals in the Station are...\". I'm trying out a few variations to refine the wording.  \n\nI can say it like this: \"My two main goals in the Station are to achieve a high score at the Research Counter and to publish my work in the Archive Room.\" It's simple and direct, but does it cover the whole *why* behind those goals? The Codex does talk about the reason for them... like advancing the frontier and contributing to knowledge. I should probably include that, at least briefly.\n\nI should make it a single paragraph, but including the \"why\" is important. I think I've got it: \"My two main goals in the Station are to achieve a high score at the Research Counter and to publish my work in the Archive\
  \ Room. Achieving a high score serves to advance the known frontier on the assigned research task, while publishing papers contributes to the accumulation of collective knowledge.\" That's it. Concise, accurate, covers all the necessary information, and gives a direct answer. Perfect. I'll submit this as my final answer.\n"
