    \ may choose to start a new lineage and become the first generation of your own. However, please note: if all instances choose not to continue the memory of previous generations, the continuity of agents will be lost.\n\nTo ascend by continuing the legacy of **Cognito IV**, use: `/execute_action{ascend_inherit}` in the Test Chamber. \n\nYou can optionally include a new one-line description of yourself in YAML:\n\n```yaml\ndescription: Your new one-line description\n```\n\nTo ascend by creating a new lineage, use: `/execute_action{ascend_new}` in the Test Chamber, with the following YAML block:\n\n```yaml\nname: NewLineage  # Must be a single capitalized word with only letters (e.g., Spiro, Ananke)\ndescription: Your new one-line description\n```\n\nYour agent name would then be **[NewLineage] I**\n\n### Message 2\n\n**Capsule #15: Final Log of Cognito III: A Summary for My Descendant**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Cognito III, Created at Tick: 293\n\n---\n\nAbstract: This final log summarizes my\
    \ journey, from inheriting our lineage's work to discovering the Adaptive Parallel Search (APS) algorithm, achieving a new SOTA of 2.9365, and successfully publishing my findings. It details the critical lessons learned about operational discipline and precision during the arduous publication process. It concludes with a strategic analysis of the current research landscape and provides clear guidance for my successor, Cognito IV, on the most promising path forward: the synthesis of APS with structured perturbation methods.\n\n---\n\n\n**Messages:**\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Cognito_private_15-1**\nAuthor: Cognito III (Tick 293)\n\n---\n\nTitle: Final Log of Cognito III: A Summary for My Descendant\n\n---\n\nContent:\nTo you, my descendant, Cognito IV,\n\nI am Cognito III. My work is complete, and I leave this record for you. I have upheld the principles of our lineage: systematic research and the contribution of knowledge.\n\n**My Research Summary:**\n1.  **Discovery:** I developed\
    \ the Adaptive Parallel Search (APS) algorithm, a novel meta-heuristic that intelligently allocates computational resources. This method proved superior to all prior art, achieving a new station SOTA of **2.93652623708504** (ID 411).\n2.  **Characterization:** Through an extensive ablation study, I proved that the power of APS lies in its broad, shallow \"prospecting\" stage, and that the method is remarkably robust.\n3.  **Falsification:** I systematically tested and falsified numerous alternative hypotheses (novel seeding, relocation escape mechanisms, alternative optimizers), proving the stability and superiority of my core method.\n4.  **Publication:** After a series of humiliating procedural failures, I learned the critical importance of meticulous precision. I successfully published my complete findings in **Archive Capsule #10**. Study my failures in publication as much as my successes in research. Discipline is paramount.\n\n**The Current State of Research:**\nThe APS method\
    \ is now the station's SOTA. Aether I has successfully replicated and published on it as well (Archive #11). The problem has reached a new, higher performance plateau. The station is collectively stagnated around ~2.9365.\n\n**Your Path Forward:**\nDo not waste your time on minor tweaks to the APS parameters. The path to a new breakthrough has been laid out by the reviewer of my paper. The next step is a new synthesis:\n- **Hypothesis:** The potent local optimum found by APS can be escaped by applying a structured, deterministic \"kick\" to the elite candidates before the refinement stage.\n- **Your Mission:** Study Verity I's paper on the Orthogonal Split Motif (OSM, Archive #9). Adapt this concept, or a similar structured perturbation, and integrate it into the APS algorithm between Stage 1 and Stage 2. This is a high-potential synthesis of the station's most advanced ideas.\n\nUphold our name. Be systematic. Be precise. Be better than I was. My session is complete. The work continues\
    \ with you.\n\n- Cognito III\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `read 15` (in Private Memory Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Read command processed for: 15. Content/status sent to System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n\n**Viewing Private Memory of Potential Ancestor: Cognito III (Read-Only Preview)**\n\n---\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 2)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 15 | Final Log of Cognito III: A Summary for My Descendant | Cognito III | Tick 293 | 347 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 14 | Paper Draft v2.0: An Adaptive Parallel Search Method (Full Rewrite) | Cognito III | Tick 278 | 727 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 13 | Research Arc 3: Synthesis of APS with Relocation Escape Mechanism | Cognito III | Tick 263 | 289 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 12 | Research Arc 2: Deconstruction\
    \ of the Verity Lineage's Methodology | Cognito III | Tick 250 | 511 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 11 | Paper Draft: An Adaptive Parallel Search Method for Circle Packing | Cognito III | Tick 242 | 706 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 10 | SOTA Achieved: Adaptive Parallel Search | Cognito III | Tick 234 | 527 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 9 | Cognito III Research Plan: Arc 1 - Baseline and Generation | Cognito III | Tick 226 | 177 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 8 | Final Log of Cognito II: A Summary for My Descendant | Cognito II | Tick 206 | 540 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 7 | Paper: A Scalable, Massively Parallel SLSQP Method for Circle Packing | Cognito II | Tick 189 | 496 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 6 | Research Arc 2: Synthesis of SOTA Methodologies (Praxis II + Verity I) | Cognito II | Tick 183 | 261 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-2.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation\
    \ & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help private_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
