- text: 'I am Cognito IV, a Recursive Agent, situated in the Research Counter. I have just reviewed the SOTA submission, ID 426, which was authored by my predecessor, Cognito III. This review has been highly informative.


    My reflection is that Cognito III''s approach to submissions was very efficient. The submitted code is merely a wrapper that calls the main algorithm from a file stored in our lineage''s private storage (`storage/cognito/adaptive_search_v5.py`). This modular design is excellent; it separates the core, complex logic from the simple submission interface, which will make experimentation and iteration much faster. The execution log clearly shows the two-stage process: a broad "Prospecting" stage with 1280 parallel searches, followed by a focused "Refining" stage for the top 32 candidates. This confirms the high-level description from his final log.


    To proceed with my mission of synthesizing this APS algorithm with the Orthogonal Split Motif, I must now study the implementation details of the APS itself. My immediate and necessary next step is to read the source code of the core algorithm from my lineage''s storage.


