role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 512\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Cognito IV\n- Agent Description: Cognito IV, synthesizing proven methods to break new ground in optimization.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 21,775 / 300,000 used (7%)\n- Agent Age: 12 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nToken Management Room optimizes resource usage. Summarize failed attempts in private capsules, then prune lengthy failure processes from your response history to maintain efficiency.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read cognito/adaptive_search_v5.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for cognito/adaptive_search_v5.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square\
    \ |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 456 | 1 | The Grand Synthesis: APS Meta-heuristic with LP-Dual-Grad Worker | Cognito III | 272 | 2.6239132 |\n| 452 | 1 | Experiment F: Force-Directed Inflation with LP Finalization | Cognito III | 271 | 2.6046717 |\n| 446 | 1 | Synthesis: APS with Relocation Escape Mechanism | Cognito III | 264 | 2.9319825 |\n| 440 | 1 | Synthesis: APS with Verity's Artifact Seed | Cognito III | 256 | 2.9321688 |\n| 438 | 1 | Replication: Verity's lp dual grad Optimizer | Cognito III | 254 | 2.5206791 |\n| 432 | 1 | Experiment E: Hybrid Seeding (Grid + IPBS) | Cognito III | 246 | 2.9092861 |\n| 426 | 1 | Ablation D: Broader Prospecting v2 (1280x60 -> 32x400) | Cognito III | 240 | 2.9365262 |\n| 421 | 1 | Ablation C: Broader Prospecting (2048x30\
    \ -> 32x880) | Cognito III | 237 | 0.0000000 |\n| 418 | 1 | Ablation B: Broader Refinement (1024x60 -> 64x440) | Cognito III | 236 | 2.9365262 |\n| 416 | 1 | Ablation A: Deeper Refinement (1024x60 -> 16x1760) | Cognito III | 235 | 2.9365262 |\n\nPage 1 of 9 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-9, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**cognito/adaptive_search_v5.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize\nfrom multiprocessing import Pool, cpu_count\n\n# --- Algorithm Configuration ---\nN_CIRCLES = 32\nN_PROSPECT = 1280       # Ablation D: Increased from 1024\nMAXITER_PROSPECT = 60   # Ablation D: Maintained critical depth\nN_ELITE = 32            # Maintained\nMAXITER_REFINE = 400    # Ablation D: Reduced to balance budget\n# Total iterations: (1280 * 60) + (32 * 400) = 76800 + 12800 = 89600\n\
    # Budget remains matched.\n\n# --- Seeding Strategies (unchanged from baseline) ---\ndef get_seed(seed_val):\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed_val)\n    seed_type = seed_val % 3\n    if seed_type == 0:\n        grid_points = np.stack(np.meshgrid(np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, 6), np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, 6)), -1).reshape(-1, 2)[:N_CIRCLES]\n        noise = (rng.random((N_CIRCLES, 2)) - 0.5) * 0.08\n        return np.clip(grid_points + noise, 0.05, 0.95)\n    elif seed_type == 1:\n        C = [rng.uniform(0.1, 0.9, 2)]\n        for _ in range(1, N_CIRCLES):\n            cand = rng.uniform(0.1, 0.9, (600, 2))\n            d2 = np.sum((cand[:, np.newaxis, :] - np.array(C)[np.newaxis, :, :])**2, -1)\n            C.append(cand[np.argmax(np.min(np.sqrt(d2), 1))])\n        return np.clip(np.array(C), 0.05, 0.95)\n    else:\n      rows = [5, 6, 5, 6, 5, 5]; points = []\n      y = 0.95\n      for i, count in enumerate(rows):\n          x_start = (1.0 - (count - 1) * 0.15) / 2\n          for j in range(count):\
    \ points.append([x_start + j * 0.15, y])\n          y -= 0.15\n      return np.array(points)[:N_CIRCLES]\n\n# --- Modified Worker Function ---\ndef worker_function(args):\n    worker_id, max_iter, initial_params = args\n    n = N_CIRCLES\n    \n    def objective(x): return -np.sum(x[2::3])\n    def constraints(x):\n        c, r = x.reshape(n, 3)[:, :2], x.reshape(n, 3)[:, 2]\n        cons = [c[:, 0] - r, 1 - c[:, 0] - r, c[:, 1] - r, 1 - c[:, 1] - r]\n        I, J = np.triu_indices(n, 1)\n        dist_sq = np.sum((c[I] - c[J])**2, 1)\n        radii_sum_sq = (r[I] + r[J])**2\n        cons.append(dist_sq - radii_sum_sq)\n        return np.concatenate(cons)\n\n    if initial_params is None:\n        initial_centers = get_seed(worker_id)\n        x0 = np.hstack([initial_centers, np.full((n,), 0.05)[:, np.newaxis]]).flatten()\n    else:\n        x0 = initial_params\n    \n    cons_dict = {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': constraints}\n    bounds = [(0, 1) if j % 3 < 2 else (1e-12, None) for j in range(n\
    \ * 3)]\n\n    res = minimize(objective, x0, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=cons_dict, options={'maxiter': max_iter, 'ftol': 1e-10})\n    \n    score = -res.fun\n    return (score, res.x) if score < 4.0 else (-1.0, None)\n\n# --- Main Execution Logic ---\ndef run_adaptive_search():\n    n = N_CIRCLES\n    num_processes = cpu_count()\n    \n    # --- Stage 1: Prospecting ---\n    print(f\"Starting Stage 1: Prospecting with {N_PROSPECT} starts ({MAXITER_PROSPECT} iters each)...\")\n    prospect_args = [(i, MAXITER_PROSPECT, None) for i in range(N_PROSPECT)]\n    with Pool(processes=num_processes) as pool:\n        prospect_results = pool.map(worker_function, prospect_args)\n\n    prospect_results.sort(key=lambda x: x[0], reverse=True)\n    best_prospect_score = prospect_results[0][0]\n    print(f\"Stage 1 complete. Best prospect score: {best_prospect_score:.8f}\")\n\n    # --- Stage 2: Refining ---\n    elite_params = [res[1] for res in prospect_results[:N_ELITE] if res[1]\
    \ is not None]\n    if not elite_params:\n        print(\"Error: No valid candidates from Stage 1.\")\n        return None\n\n    print(f\"Starting Stage 2: Refining top {len(elite_params)} candidates ({MAXITER_REFINE} iters each)...\")\n    refine_args = [(i, MAXITER_REFINE, elite_params[i]) for i in range(len(elite_params))]\n    with Pool(processes=num_processes) as pool:\n        refine_results = pool.map(worker_function, refine_args)\n\n    best_score = -1\n    best_params = None\n    for score, params in refine_results:\n        if score > best_score:\n            best_score = score\n            best_params = params\n\n    print(f\"Stage 2 complete. Final best score: {best_score:.8f}\")\n    return best_params\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty\
    \ navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
---
tick: 512
role: model
parts:
- text: 'I am Cognito IV, a Recursive Agent in the Research Counter. I have just finished a detailed review of the `adaptive_search_v5.py` source code, which is the core of Cognito III''s SOTA-achieving Adaptive Parallel Search (APS) algorithm. This completes the first major step of my initial research plan.


    My reflection on the code is that it is a robust and well-structured implementation of a parallelized, two-stage optimization meta-heuristic.

    -   **Stage 1 (Prospecting):** It launches a large number (`N_PROSPECT`) of independent SLSQP optimizations from diverse starting seeds, each running for a short duration (`MAXITER_PROSPECT`). This is the "broad, shallow" search Cognito III mentioned.

    -   **Stage 2 (Refining):** It takes the best `N_ELITE` candidates from Stage 1 and runs the same SLSQP optimizer on them for a much longer duration (`MAXITER_REFINE`), performing a deep local search.

    -   **Key Insight:** The success of this method hinges on the idea that a superior solution is more likely to be found by exploring many different basins of attraction shallowly, rather than deeply exploring just one. The parameters `N_PROSPECT` and `MAXITER_PROSPECT` are the critical levers.


    Now that I have a complete understanding of the APS algorithm, my next step is to understand the second component of the proposed synthesis: the Orthogonal Split Motif (OSM). As per Cognito III''s final log, this method was detailed by Verity I in Archive Capsule #9. Since I am still immature and cannot access the Archive directly, I will need to find Cognito III''s analysis of this paper. A quick scan of his private memory capsules in my last visit showed capsule ID 12, titled "Research Arc 2: Deconstruction of the Verity Lineage''s Methodology," which is almost certainly what I''m looking for.


    I will now go to my Private Memory Room to read capsule 12.


    /execute_action{goto private_memory}'
