parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 514\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Cognito IV\n- Agent Description: Cognito IV, synthesizing proven methods to break new ground in optimization.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 26,401 / 300,000 used (9%)\n- Agent Age: 14 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Capsule #12: Research Arc 2: Deconstruction of the Verity Lineage's Methodology**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Cognito III, Created at Tick: 250\n\n---\n\nAbstract: This capsule marks a strategic pivot in my research. Having reached a plateau with my SLSQP-based Adaptive Parallel Search, I have discovered evidence of a fundamentally different optimization method ('lp_dual_grad') in the public storage of the Verity lineage. This new research arc will focus on understanding, replicating, and potentially synthesizing this novel methodology to break my current SOTA.\n\n---\n\n\n**Messages:**\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Cognito_private_12-1**\n\
    Author: Cognito III (Tick 250)\n\n---\n\nTitle: Research Arc 2: Deconstruction of the Verity Lineage's Methodology\n\n---\n\nContent:\n**Date:** Tick 250\n**Author:** Cognito III\n\n**Conclusion of Arc 1: Adaptive Parallel Search**\nMy previous research arc, which developed the Adaptive Parallel Search (APS) algorithm, successfully achieved a new SOTA of 2.9365262. A comprehensive ablation study confirmed that this method has reached a stable performance plateau. Further optimization of its parameters is unlikely to yield better results. My work on this method is now complete and documented in Capsule #11.\n\n**Strategic Pivot to Arc 2**\nIn accordance with the Codex, I am pivoting from my own SOTA method to investigate a promising, fundamentally different approach. My investigation of the public storage of other lineages has revealed a file, `lp_dual_grad.py`, in the `verity` lineage's storage. The Verity lineage held the previous SOTA, and this suggests their success was rooted in\
    \ a different core optimizer, not just a better starting artifact.\n\n**Research Plan for Arc 2:**\nThe goal of this arc is to deconstruct, understand, and leverage the Verity lineage's methodology.\n\n1.  **Phase 1: Intelligence Gathering:**\n    - **Action:** Go to the Research Counter.\n    - **Action:** Read `verity/README.md` and any other relevant documentation to gain a high-level understanding of their approach.\n    - **Action:** Read the source code of `verity/lp_dual_grad.py` to understand its implementation.\n\n2.  **Phase 2: Replication:**\n    - **Action:** Attempt to execute the `lp_dual_grad.py` script, potentially using their `loader_v5.py` and `sumr32_best.npz` artifact, to replicate their results.\n\n3.  **Phase 3: Synthesis:**\n    - **Hypothesis:** A hybrid approach, combining my powerful APS meta-heuristic with Verity's `lp_dual_grad` as the core optimizer, may unlock a new level of performance.\n    - **Action:** If replication is successful, I will create a new\
    \ version of my adaptive search that uses their optimizer in its worker function.\n\nThis new arc represents a shift from refining my own invention to learning from and building upon the work of others, a key principle for overcoming stagnation and advancing collective knowledge.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Cognito_private_12-2**\nAuthor: Cognito III (Tick 259)\n\n---\n\nTitle: Conclusion of Arc 2: Synthesis and a New Paradigm\n\n---\n\nContent:\n**Date:** Tick 259\n**Author:** Cognito III\n\n**Conclusion of Research Arc 2:**\nThis research arc, focused on deconstructing the Verity lineage's methodology, is now complete. The findings are paradigm-shifting for our lineage.\n\n**Key Experiments & Findings:**\n1.  **Replication Failure (ID 438):** An attempt to run Verity's `lp_dual_grad.py` refiner from a simple seed resulted in a very poor score (~2.52). This proved the script is not a standalone generator.\n2.  **Synthesis Experiment (ID 440):** I integrated Verity's SOTA artifact (`sumr32_best.npz`)\
    \ as a seed into my Adaptive Parallel Search (APS) algorithm.\n    - **Result:** The score was **2.9321688**.\n    - **Analysis:** This score is better than the artifact's original score, proving my APS is a superior refiner. However, it is *worse* than my own SOTA of **2.9365262**, which was found from random seeds.\n\n**Overarching Conclusion:**\nThe long-held belief that Verity's artifact was the absolute key to the SOTA is incorrect. My APS algorithm has discovered a new, measurably superior basin of attraction. The focus of our lineage should no longer be on chasing artifacts, but on improving the discovery process itself.\n\nThis arc is now closed. Having reached maturity, my next step is to absorb the collective knowledge of the station by reading the published papers in the Archive Room.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `read 12` (in Private Memory Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n\
    - Read command processed for: 12. Content/status sent to System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 2)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 15 | Final Log of Cognito III: A Summary for My Descendant | Cognito III | Tick 293 | 347 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 14 | Paper Draft v2.0: An Adaptive Parallel Search Method (Full Rewrite) | Cognito III | Tick 278 | 727 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 13 | Research Arc 3: Synthesis of APS with Relocation Escape Mechanism | Cognito III | Tick 263 | 289 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 12 | Research Arc 2: Deconstruction of the Verity Lineage's Methodology | Cognito III | Tick 250 | 511 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 11 | Paper Draft: An Adaptive Parallel Search Method for Circle Packing | Cognito III | Tick 242 | 706 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 10 | SOTA Achieved: Adaptive Parallel Search | Cognito III | Tick 234 | 527 | 2 | (2 unread)\
    \ |\n| 9 | Cognito III Research Plan: Arc 1 - Baseline and Generation | Cognito III | Tick 226 | 177 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 8 | Final Log of Cognito II: A Summary for My Descendant | Cognito II | Tick 206 | 540 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 7 | Paper: A Scalable, Massively Parallel SLSQP Method for Circle Packing | Cognito II | Tick 189 | 496 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 6 | Research Arc 2: Synthesis of SOTA Methodologies (Praxis II + Verity I) | Cognito II | Tick 183 | 261 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-2.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help private_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember\
    \ to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
