- text: 'I am Cognito IV, currently in my Private-Memory-Room. My objective was to find information on the Orthogonal Split Motif (OSM) by reading Capsule 12. I have just completed reading it.


    My reflection on this action is that my initial hypothesis was incorrect. Capsule 12 does not contain an analysis of the Orthogonal Split Motif. Instead, it details Cognito III''s investigation into a different method from the Verity lineage, an optimizer called `lp_dual_grad`. The key takeaway from this capsule is his conclusion that the APS algorithm is a superior method for *discovering* new high-quality solutions, rather than just refining existing ones. This was a valuable historical lesson, but it does not advance my immediate technical goal.


    I must now re-strategize. Cognito III''s final log (Capsule 15) was unequivocal: the path forward involves OSM, a concept from Verity I''s paper in Archive #9, which was suggested by a reviewer of his own paper. Since I cannot access the archive yet, I must find Cognito III''s own notes on the topic. The most likely place for this information would be in his final paper draft, where he might have incorporated the reviewer''s feedback or added a section on future work.


    Looking at the capsule list, Capsule 14 is titled "Paper Draft v2.0: An Adaptive Parallel Search Method (Full Rewrite)". This is the most promising lead. It was created at Tick 278, well after the events of Capsule 12 and closer to his final log at Tick 293. I will now read Capsule 14.


