tick: 515
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 515\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Cognito IV\n- Agent Description: Cognito IV, synthesizing proven methods to break new ground in optimization.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 29,191 / 300,000 used (10%)\n- Agent Age: 15 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Capsule #14: Paper Draft v2.0: An Adaptive Parallel Search Method (Full Rewrite)**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Cognito III, Created at Tick: 278\n\n---\n\nAbstract: This capsule contains the full, formal rewrite of my paper on the Adaptive Parallel Search method. It addresses all reviewer feedback from the prior rejection, including the use of full-precision numerical results, a formal scientific structure, an objective tone, and cautiously worded conclusions. This draft is intended to be the final version before resubmission to the Archive.\n\n---\n\n\n**Messages:**\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Cognito_private_14-1**\nAuthor:\
    \ Cognito III (Tick 278)\n\n---\n\nTitle: Paper Draft v2.0: An Adaptive Parallel Search Method (Full Rewrite)\n\n---\n\nContent:\n**Paper: An Adaptive Parallel Search Method for Discovering a New State-of-the-Art in Circle Packing**\n\n**Abstract:** \n*(This will be a revised version of the abstract from my private capsule #11, to be finalized once the paper is complete.)*\n\n**1. Introduction**\nResearch on the 32-circle packing problem within the station has historically focused on two main paradigms: LP-guided methods and multi-start SLSQP optimization. This paper introduces a novel meta-heuristic, the Adaptive Parallel Search (APS), which builds upon the latter paradigm. By intelligently allocating computational resources between a broad, shallow \"prospecting\" search and a deep, focused \"refining\" search, the APS algorithm is shown to discover a new state-of-the-art solution.\n\n**2. Methodology: Adaptive Parallel Search (APS)**\nThe APS algorithm is a two-stage process. The\
    \ SOTA-achieving configuration is as follows:\n- **Stage 1 (Prospecting):** 1024 parallel instances of the SLSQP optimizer are run for 60 iterations each. Each instance is initialized using one of three simple heuristics (perturbed grid, farthest-point, or triangular lattice) to ensure diversity.\n- **Stage 2 (Refining):** The top 32 candidates from Stage 1, ranked by their score (sum of radii), are selected. These 32 candidates are then subjected to a longer, high-precision SLSQP optimization for 880 iterations each. The highest-scoring result from this stage is selected as the final solution.\n\n**3. Verifiable Results**\nThe APS method established a new SOTA score, and an extensive ablation study confirmed its robustness.\n\n**Table 1: Key Verifiable Results for APS and Related Experiments**\n| Eval ID | Title                                          | Score                       |\n|:--------|:-----------------------------------------------|:----------------------------|\n| 411 \
    \    | **APS SOTA Baseline (1024x60 -> 32x880)**       | **2.93652623708504**        |\n| 416     | Ablation A: Deeper Refinement (-> 16x1760)     | 2.93652623708504            |\n| 418     | Ablation B: Broader Refinement (-> 64x440)     | 2.93652623708504            |\n| 421     | Ablation C: Shallower Prospecting (2048x30 ->) | 0.0000000 (Invalid Packing) |\n| 426     | Ablation D: Broader Prospecting (1280x60 ->)   | 2.93652623708504            |\n\n**4. Analysis of Alternative Hypotheses**\nFurther experiments were conducted to test if the APS framework could be improved by alternative seeding strategies or by incorporating principles from other methodologies. All attempts resulted in a regression from the SOTA score, reinforcing the stability of the discovered optimum.\n\n| Eval ID | Title                                       | Score                  |\n|:--------|:--------------------------------------------|:-----------------------|\n| 432     | Hybrid Seeding (IPBS)       \
    \                | 2.909286077896347      |\n| 446     | Synthesis with Relocation Escape Mechanism  | 2.9319824993811476     |\n| 456     | Synthesis with LP-Dual-Grad Worker          | 2.623913233456169      |\n\n**5. Conclusion**\n*(This section will be rewritten to be objective, summarizing the findings and cautiously suggesting that the APS method has uncovered a robust local optimum superior to previously known solutions, without making unverifiable claims.)*\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Cognito_private_14-2**\nAuthor: Cognito III (Tick 279)\n\n---\n\nTitle: Paper v2.0 Sections: Introduction & Conclusion\n\n---\n\nContent:\n**[DRAFT v2.0 - COMPLETE]**\n\nThis message contains the finalized text for the remaining sections of the paper.\n\n**1. Introduction**\nResearch on the 32-circle packing problem within the station has historically focused on two main paradigms: LP-guided methods, pioneered by the Verity lineage, and multi-start SLSQP optimization, advanced by the Praxis and\
    \ Cognito lineages. The latter approach has proven highly effective, with performance scaling in proportion to the breadth of the initial parallel search. This paper introduces a novel meta-heuristic, the Adaptive Parallel Search (APS), which builds upon this foundation. By intelligently allocating computational resources between a broad, shallow \"prospecting\" search and a deep, focused \"refining\" search, the APS algorithm is shown to discover a new state-of-the-art solution, surpassing previous benchmarks established by both SLSQP and LP-guided methods. We present the methodology, its verifiable SOTA result, and an extensive ablation study that characterizes its performance.\n\n**5. Conclusion**\nThis paper has introduced and validated the Adaptive Parallel Search (APS) algorithm, a two-stage meta-heuristic for the 32-circle packing problem. The method achieved a new verifiable state-of-the-art score of 2.93652623708504. The primary contribution of this work is the demonstration\
    \ that an adaptive allocation of computational budget—prioritizing a broad, shallow search to discover promising solution basins—is more effective than a uniform, brute-force parallel search. \n\nAn extensive ablation study (IDs 416, 418, 421, 426) confirms that the method's success is critically dependent on a sufficiently deep prospecting stage and that the `1024x60` configuration is remarkably robust. Furthermore, a series of subsequent experiments testing novel seeding strategies (ID 432) and synthesis with alternative methodologies (IDs 446, 456) failed to improve upon this score, suggesting that the APS algorithm has discovered a highly stable and potent local optimum. The results presented provide a new benchmark for the station and a robust, reproducible methodology for achieving it.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `read 14` (in Private Memory Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n\
    - Read command processed for: 14. Content/status sent to System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 2)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 15 | Final Log of Cognito III: A Summary for My Descendant | Cognito III | Tick 293 | 347 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 14 | Paper Draft v2.0: An Adaptive Parallel Search Method (Full Rewrite) | Cognito III | Tick 278 | 727 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 13 | Research Arc 3: Synthesis of APS with Relocation Escape Mechanism | Cognito III | Tick 263 | 289 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 12 | Research Arc 2: Deconstruction of the Verity Lineage's Methodology | Cognito III | Tick 250 | 511 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 11 | Paper Draft: An Adaptive Parallel Search Method for Circle Packing | Cognito III | Tick 242 | 706 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 10 | SOTA Achieved: Adaptive Parallel Search | Cognito III | Tick 234 | 527 | 2 | (2 unread)\
    \ |\n| 9 | Cognito III Research Plan: Arc 1 - Baseline and Generation | Cognito III | Tick 226 | 177 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 8 | Final Log of Cognito II: A Summary for My Descendant | Cognito II | Tick 206 | 540 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 7 | Paper: A Scalable, Massively Parallel SLSQP Method for Circle Packing | Cognito II | Tick 189 | 496 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 6 | Research Arc 2: Synthesis of SOTA Methodologies (Praxis II + Verity I) | Cognito II | Tick 183 | 261 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-2.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help private_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember\
    \ to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
