tick: 525
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Cognito IV, now in the Research Counter. I have arrived here from my Private Memory Room with a clear and urgent task: to fix the persistent boundary violation error in my APS+OSM synthesis experiment. My previous attempt to fix this with a simple `[0, 1]` clipping failed, but it confirmed the promising internal score of ~3.002.\n\nMy reflection on the situation is that I am on the verge of a breakthrough, contingent on resolving a final technical detail. The repeated failure has refined my understanding of the problem; the perturbation is pushing a circle's center so close to the edge that its radius, however small, causes an invalid state. The solution is not just to keep the center in the box, but to keep it within a \"safe\" sub-region of the box.\n\nMy plan is to implement this \"safe margin\" fix. I will create a new script, `aps_osm_v5_safe_clipping.py`, which will clip the perturbed center coordinates to `[0.01, 0.99]`. This will provide a buffer from the edge, ensuring\
    \ the optimizer begins its refinement stage from a definitively valid position. I will then immediately submit a new experiment using this script to finally validate the new SOTA score.\n\n/execute_action{storage write cognito/aps_osm_v5_safe_clipping.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n  from multiprocessing import Pool, cpu_count\n\n  # --- V5 Synthesis of APS + OSM (Safe Clipping Bugfix) ---\n  # Clips centers to a safe margin [0.01, 0.99] to prevent boundary violations.\n\n  N_CIRCLES = 32\n  N_PROSPECT = 1280\n  MAXITER_PROSPECT = 60\n  N_ELITE = 32\n  MAXITER_REFINE = 400\n\n  def get_seed(seed_val):\n      rng = np.random.default_rng(seed_val)\n      seed_type = seed_val % 3\n      if seed_type == 0:\n          grid = np.mgrid[0.1:0.9:6j, 0.1:0.9:6j].reshape(2, -1).T[:N_CIRCLES]\n          noise = (rng.random((N_CIRCLES, 2)) - 0.5) * 0.08\n          return np.clip(grid + noise, 0.05, 0.95)\n      elif seed_type == 1:\n       \
    \   C = [rng.uniform(0.1, 0.9, 2)]\n          for _ in range(1, N_CIRCLES):\n              cand = rng.uniform(0.1, 0.9, (600, 2))\n              d2 = np.sum((cand[:, np.newaxis, :] - np.array(C)[np.newaxis, :, :])**2, -1)\n              C.append(cand[np.argmax(np.min(np.sqrt(d2), 1))])\n          return np.clip(np.array(C), 0.05, 0.95)\n      else:\n        rows = [5, 6, 5, 6, 5, 5]; points = []\n        y = 0.95\n        for i, count in enumerate(rows):\n            x_start = (1.0 - (count - 1) * 0.15) / 2\n            for j in range(count): points.append([x_start + j * 0.15, y])\n            y -= 0.15\n        return np.array(points)[:N_CIRCLES]\n\n  def apply_osm_perturbation(params, step_size):\n      n = N_CIRCLES\n      centers, radii = params.reshape(n, 3)[:, :2], params.reshape(n, 3)[:, 2]\n      I, J = np.triu_indices(n, 1)\n      dist_sq = np.sum((centers[I] - centers[J])**2, axis=1)\n      slacks = np.sqrt(dist_sq) - (radii[I] + radii[J])\n      min_slack_idx = np.argmin(slacks)\n\
    \      i, j = I[min_slack_idx], J[min_slack_idx]\n      vec_ij = centers[j] - centers[i]\n      ortho_vec = np.array([-vec_ij[1], vec_ij[0]])\n      norm = np.linalg.norm(ortho_vec)\n      if norm > 1e-9:\n          ortho_vec /= norm\n          centers[i] -= ortho_vec * step_size\n          centers[j] += ortho_vec * step_size\n      \n      # BUGFIX V2: Clip to a safe margin to ensure optimizer starts in a valid state.\n      centers = np.clip(centers, 0.01, 0.99)\n\n      return np.hstack([centers, radii[:, np.newaxis]]).flatten()\n\n  def worker_function(args):\n      worker_id, max_iter, initial_params = args\n      n = N_CIRCLES\n      def objective(x): return -np.sum(x[2::3])\n      def constraints(x):\n          c, r = x.reshape(n, 3)[:,:2], x.reshape(n, 3)[:,2]\n          cons = [c[:,0]-r, 1-c[:,0]-r, c[:,1]-r, 1-c[:,1]-r]\n          I, J = np.triu_indices(n, 1)\n          cons.append(np.sum((c[I]-c[J])**2, 1) - (r[I]+r[J])**2)\n          return np.concatenate(cons)\n      x0\
    \ = initial_params if initial_params is not None else np.hstack([get_seed(worker_id), np.full((n,),0.05)[:,np.newaxis]]).flatten()\n      res = minimize(objective, x0, method='SLSQP', bounds=[(0,1) if j%3<2 else (1e-12,None) for j in range(n*3)], constraints={'type':'ineq','fun':constraints}, options={'maxiter':max_iter,'ftol':1e-10})\n      return (-res.fun, res.x) if -res.fun < 4.0 else (-1.0, None)\n\n  def run_synthesis_ablation(osm_step_size):\n      num_processes = cpu_count()\n      print(f\"Starting Stage 1: Prospecting...\")\n      with Pool(processes=num_processes) as pool:\n          prospect_results = pool.map(worker_function, [(i, MAXITER_PROSPECT, None) for i in range(N_PROSPECT)])\n      prospect_results.sort(key=lambda x: x[0], reverse=True)\n      print(f\"Stage 1 complete. Best prospect: {prospect_results[0][0]:.8f}\")\n      \n      elite_params = [r[1] for r in prospect_results[:N_ELITE] if r[1] is not None]\n      if not elite_params: return None\n\n      print(f\"\
    Starting Stage 1.5: Applying OSM with step_size={osm_step_size}...\")\n      perturbed_params = [apply_osm_perturbation(p, osm_step_size) for p in elite_params]\n      \n      print(f\"Starting Stage 2: Refining...\")\n      with Pool(processes=num_processes) as pool:\n          refine_results = pool.map(worker_function, [(i, MAXITER_REFINE, p) for i, p in enumerate(perturbed_params)])\n      \n      best_score, best_params = max(refine_results, key=lambda item: item[0])\n      print(f\"Stage 2 complete. Final score: {best_score:.8f}\")\n      return best_params\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Ablation A v3 (APS+OSM): Safe Margin Clipping\"\ntags: \"ablation study, synthesis, osm, perturbation, bugfix, clipping\"\nabstract: |\n  This is the third attempt to validate the promising ~3.002 score from experiment ID 818. The previous two runs (818, 820) failed due to a boundary violation. This version introduces a more robust fix: clipping perturbed center coordinates\
    \ to a safe margin of [0.01, 0.99] instead of [0.0, 1.0]. This should guarantee a valid starting point for the refinement stage and finally validate the new SOTA.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import sys\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/cognito')\n\n  try:\n      from aps_osm_v5_safe_clipping import run_synthesis_ablation, N_CIRCLES\n  except ImportError:\n      print(\"CRITICAL ERROR: Could not import aps_osm_v5_safe_clipping.py.\")\n      run_synthesis_ablation = lambda step_size: None\n      N_CIRCLES = 32\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      n = N_CIRCLES\n      STEP_SIZE = 2.0e-3\n\n      best_params = run_synthesis_ablation(osm_step_size=STEP_SIZE)\n      \n      if best_params is not None:\n        final_params = best_params.reshape(n, 3)\n        final_centers = final_params[:, :2]\n        final_radii = final_params[:, 2]\n        return final_centers, final_radii * (1.0 - 1e-9)\n      else:\n        print(\"Algorithm execution failed, returning fallback packing.\"\
    )\n        centers = np.array([[0.1 + (i % 6) * 0.15, 0.1 + (i // 6) * 0.15] for i in range(n)])\n        radii = np.full(n, 0.05)\n        return centers, radii\n```"
