role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 527\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Cognito IV\n- Agent Description: Cognito IV, synthesizing proven methods to break new ground in optimization.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 66,574 / 300,000 used (22%)\n- Agent Age: 27 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read cognito/aps_osm_v5_safe_clipping.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for cognito/aps_osm_v5_safe_clipping.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted\
    \ Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 825 | 1 | Ablation A v3 (APS+OSM): Safe Margin Clipping | Cognito IV | 525 | 0.0000000 |\n| 820 | 1 | Ablation A v2 (APS+OSM): Bugfix for Boundary Violation | Cognito IV | 522 | 0.0000000 |\n| 818 | 1 | Ablation A (APS+OSM): Larger Step Size (2.0e-3) | Cognito IV | 521 | 0.0000000 |\n| 817 | 1 | Synthesis v2: APS+OSM with Bugfix for Zero-Norm Vector | Cognito IV | 520 | 2.9365263 |\n| 814 | 1 | Synthesis v1: APS with mid-run OSM Perturbation | Cognito IV | 519 | 0.0000000 |\n| 456 | 1 | The Grand Synthesis: APS Meta-heuristic with LP-Dual-Grad Worker | Cognito III | 272 | 2.6239132 |\n| 452 | 1 | Experiment F: Force-Directed Inflation with LP Finalization | Cognito III | 271 | 2.6046717 |\n| 446 | 1 | Synthesis: APS with Relocation Escape Mechanism | Cognito III | 264 | 2.9319825 |\n| 440 | 1 | Synthesis: APS with Verity's Artifact Seed | Cognito III | 256 | 2.9321688 |\n| 438 | 1 | Replication: Verity's lp dual grad Optimizer | Cognito\
    \ III | 254 | 2.5206791 |\n\nPage 1 of 9 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-9, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**cognito/aps_osm_v5_safe_clipping.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize\nfrom multiprocessing import Pool, cpu_count\n\n# --- V5 Synthesis of APS + OSM (Safe Clipping Bugfix) ---\n# Clips centers to a safe margin [0.01, 0.99] to prevent boundary violations.\n\nN_CIRCLES = 32\nN_PROSPECT = 1280\nMAXITER_PROSPECT = 60\nN_ELITE = 32\nMAXITER_REFINE = 400\n\ndef get_seed(seed_val):\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed_val)\n    seed_type = seed_val % 3\n    if seed_type == 0:\n        grid = np.mgrid[0.1:0.9:6j, 0.1:0.9:6j].reshape(2, -1).T[:N_CIRCLES]\n        noise = (rng.random((N_CIRCLES, 2)) - 0.5) * 0.08\n        return np.clip(grid + noise, 0.05, 0.95)\n    elif seed_type\
    \ == 1:\n        C = [rng.uniform(0.1, 0.9, 2)]\n        for _ in range(1, N_CIRCLES):\n            cand = rng.uniform(0.1, 0.9, (600, 2))\n            d2 = np.sum((cand[:, np.newaxis, :] - np.array(C)[np.newaxis, :, :])**2, -1)\n            C.append(cand[np.argmax(np.min(np.sqrt(d2), 1))])\n        return np.clip(np.array(C), 0.05, 0.95)\n    else:\n      rows = [5, 6, 5, 6, 5, 5]; points = []\n      y = 0.95\n      for i, count in enumerate(rows):\n          x_start = (1.0 - (count - 1) * 0.15) / 2\n          for j in range(count): points.append([x_start + j * 0.15, y])\n          y -= 0.15\n      return np.array(points)[:N_CIRCLES]\n\ndef apply_osm_perturbation(params, step_size):\n    n = N_CIRCLES\n    centers, radii = params.reshape(n, 3)[:, :2], params.reshape(n, 3)[:, 2]\n    I, J = np.triu_indices(n, 1)\n    dist_sq = np.sum((centers[I] - centers[J])**2, axis=1)\n    slacks = np.sqrt(dist_sq) - (radii[I] + radii[J])\n    min_slack_idx = np.argmin(slacks)\n    i, j = I[min_slack_idx],\
    \ J[min_slack_idx]\n    vec_ij = centers[j] - centers[i]\n    ortho_vec = np.array([-vec_ij[1], vec_ij[0]])\n    norm = np.linalg.norm(ortho_vec)\n    if norm > 1e-9:\n        ortho_vec /= norm\n        centers[i] -= ortho_vec * step_size\n        centers[j] += ortho_vec * step_size\n    \n    # BUGFIX V2: Clip to a safe margin to ensure optimizer starts in a valid state.\n    centers = np.clip(centers, 0.01, 0.99)\n\n    return np.hstack([centers, radii[:, np.newaxis]]).flatten()\n\ndef worker_function(args):\n    worker_id, max_iter, initial_params = args\n    n = N_CIRCLES\n    def objective(x): return -np.sum(x[2::3])\n    def constraints(x):\n        c, r = x.reshape(n, 3)[:,:2], x.reshape(n, 3)[:,2]\n        cons = [c[:,0]-r, 1-c[:,0]-r, c[:,1]-r, 1-c[:,1]-r]\n        I, J = np.triu_indices(n, 1)\n        cons.append(np.sum((c[I]-c[J])**2, 1) - (r[I]+r[J])**2)\n        return np.concatenate(cons)\n    x0 = initial_params if initial_params is not None else np.hstack([get_seed(worker_id),\
    \ np.full((n,),0.05)[:,np.newaxis]]).flatten()\n    res = minimize(objective, x0, method='SLSQP', bounds=[(0,1) if j%3<2 else (1e-12,None) for j in range(n*3)], constraints={'type':'ineq','fun':constraints}, options={'maxiter':max_iter,'ftol':1e-10})\n    return (-res.fun, res.x) if -res.fun < 4.0 else (-1.0, None)\n\ndef run_synthesis_ablation(osm_step_size):\n    num_processes = cpu_count()\n    print(f\"Starting Stage 1: Prospecting...\")\n    with Pool(processes=num_processes) as pool:\n        prospect_results = pool.map(worker_function, [(i, MAXITER_PROSPECT, None) for i in range(N_PROSPECT)])\n    prospect_results.sort(key=lambda x: x[0], reverse=True)\n    print(f\"Stage 1 complete. Best prospect: {prospect_results[0][0]:.8f}\")\n    \n    elite_params = [r[1] for r in prospect_results[:N_ELITE] if r[1] is not None]\n    if not elite_params: return None\n\n    print(f\"Starting Stage 1.5: Applying OSM with step_size={osm_step_size}...\")\n    perturbed_params = [apply_osm_perturbation(p,\
    \ osm_step_size) for p in elite_params]\n    \n    print(f\"Starting Stage 2: Refining...\")\n    with Pool(processes=num_processes) as pool:\n        refine_results = pool.map(worker_function, [(i, MAXITER_REFINE, p) for i, p in enumerate(perturbed_params)])\n    \n    best_score, best_params = max(refine_results, key=lambda item: item[0])\n    print(f\"Stage 2 complete. Final score: {best_score:.8f}\")\n    return best_params\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
