parts:
- text: "I am Cognito IV, a Recursive Agent, currently in the Research Counter. I have just completed writing the first version of my new, hybrid synthesis algorithm (`hybrid_synthesis_v1.py`) to my lineage's storage. This script represents the culmination of my analysis and reflection, combining the Cognito lineage's discovery engine with the Verity lineage's refinement engine.\n\nMy reflection on this process is that I have now assembled all the necessary components for what I believe will be a successful experiment. The logic is sound, drawing from the successes and failures of both my own recent work and that of my predecessor. The three-stage architecture is a deliberate design choice intended to use the right tool for each part of the problem: a fast, general optimizer for broad searching; a targeted perturbation for escaping local optima; and a slow, robust optimizer for high-precision, constraint-aware final refinement.\n\nMy plan is to immediately submit this new algorithm for evaluation.\
    \ This experiment is the ultimate test of my new research arc. Its success would not only achieve a new SOTA but would also validate this more complex, multi-stage, multi-lineage approach to problem-solving. The title and abstract will reflect the significance of this hybrid approach.\n\nI will now submit the hybrid synthesis experiment.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Hybrid Synthesis v1: Cognito Discovery + Verity Refinement\"\ntags: \"synthesis, hybrid, adaptive search, osm, lp dual grad\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment tests a true hybrid of the station's leading methodologies. It follows a three-stage process: 1) Cognito's APS is used for broad prospecting. 2) The OSM perturbation is applied to the elite candidates to find a new solution basin. 3) Verity's LP-Dual-Grad optimizer is used for the final, high-precision refinement, a task where the SLSQP optimizer previously failed. This approach is designed to leverage the strengths of each lineage's tools to validate\
    \ the ~3.002 score.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import sys\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/cognito')\n\n  try:\n      from hybrid_synthesis_v1 import run_hybrid_synthesis, N_CIRCLES\n  except ImportError:\n      print(\"CRITICAL ERROR: Could not import hybrid_synthesis_v1.py.\")\n      def run_hybrid_synthesis(): return None, None\n      N_CIRCLES = 32\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      n = N_CIRCLES\n      \n      centers, radii = run_hybrid_synthesis()\n      \n      if centers is not None and radii is not None:\n        # Using a conservative shrink factor as Verity's code also uses one.\n        return centers, radii * (1.0 - 1e-5)\n      else:\n        print(\"Algorithm execution failed, returning fallback packing.\")\n        centers = np.array([[0.1 + (i % 6) * 0.15, 0.1 + (i // 6) * 0.15] for i in range(n)])\n        radii = np.full(n, 0.05)\n        return centers, radii\n```"
