tick: 538
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Cognito IV, a Recursive Agent in the Research Counter. My major hybrid synthesis experiment, ID 845, has just completed. It passed validation but produced a score of ~2.905.\n\nMy reflection on this result is that it is a significant regression. The score is not only far below the promising ~3.002 signal, but it is also substantially worse than the existing SOTA of ~2.936. My grand hypothesis—that the Verity refiner could successfully optimize the perturbed candidates where SLSQP failed—has been falsified. The experiment has passed validation, which is an improvement, but the core performance is poor.\n\nI must analyze the logic of the experiment to understand this failure.\n1.  **Stage 1 (Prospecting):** This stage uses the same SLSQP worker as my predecessor's SOTA-achieving algorithm. It should be finding candidates in the ~2.936 region.\n2.  **Stage 1.5 (Perturbation):** This stage applies the large-step OSM kick. My previous experiments showed this successfully moves candidates\
    \ into the ~3.002 region, although they are invalid.\n3.  **Stage 2 (Refinement):** This stage takes these promising but invalid starting points and hands them to the Verity LP-dual-grad refiner.\n\nThe outcome of 2.905 implies that the Verity refiner, when given these specific starting points, is not only failing to find the ~3.002 optimum but is actively moving the solution to a much worse local optimum. This is a surprising and deeply counter-intuitive result. Why would a more robust optimizer perform so poorly?\n\nThere must be a parameter mismatch. I gave the Verity refiner a `time_budget` of 30 seconds. Looking back at the `lp_dual_grad.py` source code, I see its default is 120 seconds. It's highly probable that 30 seconds is simply not enough time for this completely different, iterative LP-based method to converge. It is likely terminating prematurely and returning a suboptimal, albeit valid, solution.\n\nMy plan is to test this new hypothesis directly. I will conduct an ablation\
    \ study on the `REFINEMENT_TIME_BUDGET_PER_WORKER`. I will create a new version of the script allowing this to be configured, and I will submit an experiment that quadruples the budget to 120 seconds, matching the default in the original Verity code.\n\n/execute_action{storage write cognito/hybrid_synthesis_v2_ablation.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # V2 of the Hybrid Synthesis (Ablation Ready for time budget)\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n  from multiprocessing import Pool, cpu_count\n  import sys\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/verity')\n  try:\n      from lp_dual_grad import refine_centers\n  except ImportError:\n      def refine_centers(initial, time_budget, seed):\n          return initial, np.full(initial.shape[0], 0.01), 0.01\n\n  N_CIRCLES = 32\n  N_PROSPECT = 1280\n  MAXITER_PROSPECT = 60\n  N_ELITE = 32\n  OSM_STEP_SIZE = 2.0e-3\n  \n  def get_seed(seed_val):\n      rng = np.random.default_rng(seed_val)\n      C = [rng.uniform(0.1, 0.9, 2)];\n   \
    \   for _ in range(1, N_CIRCLES):\n          cand = rng.uniform(0.1, 0.9, (600, 2))\n          d2 = np.sum((cand[:, np.newaxis, :] - np.array(C)[np.newaxis, :, :])**2, -1)\n          C.append(cand[np.argmax(np.min(np.sqrt(d2), 1))])\n      return np.clip(np.array(C), 0.05, 0.95)\n\n  def slsqp_worker(args):\n      worker_id, max_iter, _ = args; n = N_CIRCLES\n      def objective(x): return -np.sum(x[2::3])\n      def constraints(x):\n          c, r = x.reshape(n,3)[:,:2], x.reshape(n,3)[:,2]\n          cons = [c[:,0]-r, 1-c[:,0]-r, c[:,1]-r, 1-c[:,1]-r]\n          I,J = np.triu_indices(n,1)\n          cons.append(np.sum((c[I]-c[J])**2, 1) - (r[I]+r[J])**2)\n          return np.concatenate(cons)\n      x0 = np.hstack([get_seed(worker_id), np.full((n,),0.05)[:,np.newaxis]]).flatten()\n      res = minimize(objective,x0,method='SLSQP',bounds=[(0,1) if j%3<2 else (1e-12,None) for j in range(n*3)],constraints={'type':'ineq','fun':constraints},options={'maxiter':max_iter,'ftol':1e-10})\n  \
    \    return (-res.fun, res.x)\n\n  def apply_osm_perturbation(params, step_size):\n      n = N_CIRCLES\n      centers, radii = params.reshape(n, 3)[:,:2], params.reshape(n, 3)[:,2]\n      I, J = np.triu_indices(n, 1)\n      slacks = np.sqrt(np.sum((centers[I]-centers[J])**2,axis=1)) - (radii[I]+radii[J])\n      i, j = I[np.argmin(slacks)], J[np.argmin(slacks)]\n      vec_ij = centers[j] - centers[i]\n      ortho_vec = np.array([-vec_ij[1], vec_ij[0]])\n      norm = np.linalg.norm(ortho_vec)\n      if norm > 1e-9:\n          ortho_vec /= norm\n          centers[i] -= ortho_vec * step_size\n          centers[j] += ortho_vec * step_size\n      return np.clip(centers, 0.01, 0.99)\n\n  def verity_refiner_worker(args):\n      worker_id, initial_centers, time_budget = args\n      return refine_centers(initial_centers, time_budget=time_budget, seed=worker_id)\n\n  def run_hybrid_synthesis_ablation(refinement_time_budget):\n      num_processes = cpu_count()\n      print(\"--- Stage 1: Prospecting\
    \ (SLSQP) ---\")\n      with Pool(processes=num_processes) as pool:\n          prospect_results = pool.map(slsqp_worker, [(i, MAXITER_PROSPECT, None) for i in range(N_PROSPECT)])\n      prospect_results.sort(key=lambda x: x[0], reverse=True)\n      elite_params = [r[1] for r in prospect_results[:N_ELITE] if r[1] is not None]\n      if not elite_params: return None, None\n      \n      print(\"--- Stage 1.5: Perturbing (OSM) ---\")\n      perturbed_centers = [apply_osm_perturbation(p, OSM_STEP_SIZE) for p in elite_params]\n      \n      print(f\"--- Stage 2: Refining (LP-Dual-Grad) with budget={refinement_time_budget}s ---\")\n      refine_args = [(i, perturbed_centers[i], refinement_time_budget) for i in range(len(perturbed_centers))]\n      with Pool(processes=num_processes) as pool:\n          refine_results = pool.map(verity_refiner_worker, refine_args)\n      \n      best_score, best_centers, best_radii = max(refine_results, key=lambda item: item[0])\n      print(f\"Hybrid Synthesis\
    \ Complete. Final score: {best_score:.8f}\")\n      return best_centers, best_radii\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Ablation A (Hybrid): Increase Refiner Time Budget to 120s\"\ntags: \"ablation study, hybrid, lp dual grad, time budget\"\nabstract: |\n  The initial hybrid synthesis (ID 845) yielded a poor score of ~2.905. I hypothesize this is due to an insufficient time budget (30s) for the Verity LP-dual-grad refiner, causing premature termination. This experiment tests this hypothesis by quadrupling the per-worker refinement budget to 120s, matching the default in the original Verity implementation. The goal is to see if a longer refinement time allows the optimizer to converge to the superior ~3.002 optimum.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import sys\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/cognito')\n\n  try:\n      from hybrid_synthesis_v2_ablation import run_hybrid_synthesis_ablation, N_CIRCLES\n  except ImportError:\n      print(\"CRITICAL ERROR: Could not import\
    \ hybrid_synthesis_v2_ablation.py.\")\n      def run_hybrid_synthesis_ablation(b): return None, None\n      N_CIRCLES = 32\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      n = N_CIRCLES\n      # Ablation Parameter:\n      TIME_BUDGET = 120.0\n\n      centers, radii = run_hybrid_synthesis_ablation(refinement_time_budget=TIME_BUDGET)\n      \n      if centers is not None and radii is not None:\n        return centers, radii * (1.0 - 1e-5)\n      else:\n        print(\"Algorithm execution failed, returning fallback packing.\")\n        centers = np.array([[0.1 + (i % 6) * 0.15, 0.1 + (i // 6) * 0.15] for i in range(n)])\n        radii = np.full(n, 0.05)\n        return centers, radii\n```"
