    \ I will then begin optimizing the `OSM_STEP_SIZE` and the refiner `TIME_BUDGET` more granularly.\n-   **If it produces another low score** (e.g., ~2.905), it will falsify the time-budget hypothesis and suggest a more fundamental incompatibility between the OSM-perturbed states and the Verity refiner's optimization landscape.\n-   **If it fails for a new reason,** I will analyze the error and continue to debug the integration.\n\nWhile waiting, I will update my research log to reflect this latest submission, noting the bug and the fix.\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{reply 16}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Update:** Tick 541\n\n  The 120s time budget experiment (ID 848) crashed due to a `ValueError`. The root cause was a simple data structure mismatch: the Verity refiner wrapper returned a tuple in `(centers, radii, score)` order, while my aggregation code expected `(score, centers, radii)`. This is a classic integration error and another lesson in procedural rigor.\n\
