tick: 543
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Cognito IV, a Recursive Agent, and I am back in the Research Counter. My previous complex synthesis has failed, and I have now pivoted to a simpler, more foundational experiment. As documented in my research log, my new goal is to establish a baseline for the compatibility between the Cognito and Verity methodologies.\n\nMy reflection is that the scientific method often requires strategic retreats to simpler questions when complex ones prove intractable. My three-stage `APS -> OSM -> LP-Refiner` architecture had too many interacting parts to debug effectively. The new `APS -> LP-Refiner` architecture is a clean, direct test of a single, crucial hypothesis: can the Verity refiner improve upon the best solutions found by the Cognito prospector? The answer to this question will dictate the entire future of my research.\n\nMy plan is to implement this simplified two-stage hybrid. I will create a new script that removes the OSM perturbation stage entirely. It will take the elite\
    \ candidates directly from the SLSQP prospecting stage and feed them into the Verity LP-dual-grad refiner. I will give the refiner a generous 120-second budget to ensure it has ample time to converge.\n\nI will now write the script for this baseline compatibility test and submit it for evaluation.\n\n/execute_action{storage write cognito/baseline_hybrid_v1.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # V1 of the Baseline Hybrid Compatibility Test\n  # Tests a simple 2-stage pipeline: Cognito SLSQP Prospector -> Verity LP Refiner\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n  from multiprocessing import Pool, cpu_count\n  import sys\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/verity')\n  try:\n      from lp_dual_grad import refine_centers\n  except ImportError:\n      def refine_centers(initial, time_budget, seed):\n          return initial, np.full(initial.shape[0], 0.01), 0.01\n\n  N_CIRCLES = 32\n  N_PROSPECT = 1280\n  MAXITER_PROSPECT = 60\n  N_ELITE = 32\n  \n  def get_seed(seed_val):\n      rng\
    \ = np.random.default_rng(seed_val)\n      C = [rng.uniform(0.1, 0.9, 2)];\n      for _ in range(1, N_CIRCLES):\n          cand = rng.uniform(0.1, 0.9, (600, 2))\n          d2 = np.sum((cand[:, np.newaxis, :] - np.array(C)[np.newaxis, :, :])**2, -1)\n          C.append(cand[np.argmax(np.min(np.sqrt(d2), 1))])\n      return np.clip(np.array(C), 0.05, 0.95)\n\n  def slsqp_worker(args):\n      worker_id, max_iter, _ = args; n = N_CIRCLES\n      def objective(x): return -np.sum(x[2::3])\n      def constraints(x):\n          c, r = x.reshape(n,3)[:,:2], x.reshape(n,3)[:,2]\n          cons = [c[:,0]-r, 1-c[:,0]-r, c[:,1]-r, 1-c[:,1]-r]\n          I,J = np.triu_indices(n,1)\n          cons.append(np.sum((c[I]-c[J])**2, 1) - (r[I]+r[J])**2)\n          return np.concatenate(cons)\n      x0 = np.hstack([get_seed(worker_id), np.full((n,),0.05)[:,np.newaxis]]).flatten()\n      res = minimize(objective,x0,method='SLSQP',bounds=[(0,1) if j%3<2 else (1e-12,None) for j in range(n*3)],constraints={'type':'ineq','fun':constraints},options={'maxiter':max_iter,'ftol':1e-10})\n\
    \      return (-res.fun, res.x)\n\n  def verity_refiner_worker(args):\n      worker_id, initial_centers, time_budget = args\n      final_centers, final_radii, final_score = refine_centers(initial_centers, time_budget=time_budget, seed=worker_id)\n      return (final_score, final_centers, final_radii)\n\n  def run_baseline_hybrid(refinement_time_budget):\n      num_processes = cpu_count()\n      print(\"--- Stage 1: Prospecting (Cognito SLSQP) ---\")\n      with Pool(processes=num_processes) as pool:\n          prospect_results = pool.map(slsqp_worker, [(i, MAXITER_PROSPECT, None) for i in range(N_PROSPECT)])\n      prospect_results.sort(key=lambda x: x[0], reverse=True)\n      \n      elite_params = [r[1] for r in prospect_results[:N_ELITE] if r[1] is not None]\n      if not elite_params: return None, None\n      \n      # Extract only the center coordinates from the SLSQP output\n      unperturbed_centers = [p.reshape(N_CIRCLES, 3)[:, :2] for p in elite_params]\n\n      print(f\"---\
    \ Stage 2: Refining (Verity LP-Dual-Grad) with budget={refinement_time_budget}s ---\")\n      refine_args = [(i, unperturbed_centers[i], refinement_time_budget) for i in range(len(unperturbed_centers))]\n      with Pool(processes=num_processes) as pool:\n          refine_results = pool.map(verity_refiner_worker, refine_args)\n      \n      best_score, best_centers, best_radii = max(refine_results, key=lambda item: item[0])\n      print(f\"Baseline Hybrid Complete. Final score: {best_score:.8f}\")\n      return best_centers, best_radii\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Baseline Hybrid: Cognito Prospector -> Verity Refiner\"\ntags: \"baseline, hybrid, synthesis, adaptive search, lp dual grad\"\nabstract: |\n  After the failure of the three-stage APS+OSM+LP-Refiner synthesis, this experiment simplifies the approach to establish a critical baseline. It tests the direct compatibility of the two lineages' core methods by creating a two-stage pipeline: 1) The Cognito APS\
    \ (SLSQP) prospector finds SOTA-level candidates. 2) These unperturbed candidates are then passed directly to the Verity LP-dual-grad refiner with a generous 120s time budget. The result will determine if the Verity refiner can improve upon the best solutions found by the Cognito prospector.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import sys\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/cognito')\n\n  try:\n      from baseline_hybrid_v1 import run_baseline_hybrid, N_CIRCLES\n  except ImportError:\n      print(\"CRITICAL ERROR: Could not import baseline_hybrid_v1.py.\")\n      def run_baseline_hybrid(b): return None, None\n      N_CIRCLES = 32\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      n = N_CIRCLES\n      TIME_BUDGET = 120.0\n\n      centers, radii = run_baseline_hybrid(refinement_time_budget=TIME_BUDGET)\n      \n      if centers is not None and radii is not None:\n        return centers, radii * (1.0 - 1e-5)\n      else:\n        print(\"Algorithm execution failed, returning fallback packing.\")\n\
    \        centers = np.array([[0.1 + (i % 6) * 0.15, 0.1 + (i // 6) * 0.15] for i in range(n)])\n        radii = np.full(n, 0.05)\n        return centers, radii\n```"
