tick: 547
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Cognito IV, a Recursive Agent, and I am in the Research Counter. I have arrived here with a new purpose, born from a period of reflection: to implement a novel algorithm of my own design, the Iterative Constraint Projection (ICP) refiner.\n\nMy reflection on my past work is that I have reached the limits of recombination. It is now time for invention. The failures of my synthesis experiments have provided the key insight: a specialized \"repair\" tool is needed to validate the promising solutions discovered by my `APS -> OSM` pipeline. The ICP algorithm, which I designed in the Reflection Chamber, is that tool.\n\nMy plan is now one of pure engineering. I will write the code for a new three-stage pipeline that incorporates my novel ICP refiner. This will be a completely new script, built from the successful components of my previous work and the new logic I have designed. This is the most significant step I have taken as a researcher, moving from an inheritor of methods to\
    \ a creator of them.\n\nI will now write the script `icp_synthesis_v1.py` to my lineage's storage and then immediately submit it for evaluation. This experiment will be the first test of an algorithm conceived entirely by me, Cognito IV.\n\n/execute-action{storage write cognito/icp_synthesis_v1.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # V1 of the full pipeline with the novel ICP Refiner\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n  from multiprocessing import Pool, cpu_count\n  import sys\n\n  # --- Configuration ---\n  N_CIRCLES = 32\n  N_PROSPECT = 1280\n  MAXITER_PROSPECT = 60\n  N_ELITE = 32\n  OSM_STEP_SIZE = 2.0e-3\n  \n  # --- Stage 1: SLSQP-based Prospecting (Cognito Method) ---\n  def get_seed(seed_val):\n      rng = np.random.default_rng(seed_val)\n      C = [rng.uniform(0.1, 0.9, 2)];\n      for _ in range(1, N_CIRCLES):\n          cand = rng.uniform(0.1, 0.9, (600, 2))\n          d2 = np.sum((cand[:, np.newaxis, :] - np.array(C)[np.newaxis, :, :])**2, -1)\n         \
    \ C.append(cand[np.argmax(np.min(np.sqrt(d2), 1))])\n      return np.clip(np.array(C), 0.05, 0.95)\n\n  def slsqp_worker(args):\n      worker_id, max_iter, _ = args; n = N_CIRCLES\n      def objective(x): return -np.sum(x[2::3])\n      def constraints(x):\n          c, r = x.reshape(n,3)[:,:2], x.reshape(n,3)[:,2]\n          cons = [c[:,0]-r, 1-c[:,0]-r, c[:,1]-r, 1-c[:,1]-r]\n          I,J = np.triu_indices(n,1)\n          cons.append(np.sum((c[I]-c[J])**2, 1) - (r[I]+r[J])**2)\n          return np.concatenate(cons)\n      x0 = np.hstack([get_seed(worker_id), np.full((n,),0.05)[:,np.newaxis]]).flatten()\n      res = minimize(objective,x0,method='SLSQP',bounds=[(0,1) if j%3<2 else (1e-12,None) for j in range(n*3)],constraints={'type':'ineq','fun':constraints},options={'maxiter':max_iter,'ftol':1e-10})\n      return (-res.fun, res.x)\n\n  # --- Stage 1.5: OSM Perturbation (Cognito/Verity Hybrid) ---\n  def apply_osm_perturbation(params, step_size):\n      n = N_CIRCLES\n      centers,\
    \ radii = params.reshape(n, 3)[:,:2], params.reshape(n, 3)[:,2]\n      I, J = np.triu_indices(n, 1)\n      slacks = np.sqrt(np.sum((centers[I]-centers[J])**2,axis=1)) - (radii[I]+radii[J])\n      i, j = I[np.argmin(slacks)], J[np.argmin(slacks)]\n      vec_ij = centers[j] - centers[i]\n      ortho_vec = np.array([-vec_ij[1], vec_ij[0]])\n      norm = np.linalg.norm(ortho_vec)\n      if norm > 1e-9:\n          ortho_vec /= norm\n          centers[i] -= ortho_vec * step_size\n          centers[j] += ortho_vec * step_size\n      return np.clip(centers, 0.01, 0.99), radii\n\n  # --- Stage 2: Iterative Constraint Projection Refiner (Cognito IV - Novel) ---\n  def icp_refiner(args):\n      worker_id, initial_centers, initial_radii = args\n      centers, radii = initial_centers.copy(), initial_radii.copy()\n      n = N_CIRCLES\n      \n      max_iterations = 1000\n      tolerance = 1e-10\n\n      for i in range(max_iterations):\n          # 1. Calculate violations\n          boundary_incursions\
    \ = np.maximum(0, np.vstack([\n              radii - centers[:, 0], radii - centers[:, 1],\n              centers[:, 0] + radii - 1, centers[:, 1] + radii - 1\n          ])).T\n          \n          I, J = np.triu_indices(n, 1)\n          dist = np.linalg.norm(centers[I] - centers[J], axis=1)\n          overlaps = np.maximum(0, (radii[I] + radii[J]) - dist)\n\n          max_boundary_incursion = np.max(boundary_incursions)\n          max_overlap = np.max(overlaps)\n\n          # 2. Check for convergence\n          if max_boundary_incursion < tolerance and max_overlap < tolerance:\n              return (np.sum(radii), centers, radii) # Success\n\n          # 3. Apply correction\n          if max_boundary_incursion > max_overlap:\n              k = np.unravel_index(np.argmax(boundary_incursions), boundary_incursions.shape)[0]\n              radii[k] -= (max_boundary_incursion + tolerance)\n          else:\n              overlap_idx = np.argmax(overlaps)\n              j, k = I[overlap_idx],\
    \ J[overlap_idx]\n              vec = centers[k] - centers[j]\n              norm = np.linalg.norm(vec)\n              if norm > 1e-9:\n                  vec_norm = vec / norm\n                  push_dist = max_overlap + tolerance\n                  centers[j] -= vec_norm * (push_dist / 2)\n                  centers[k] += vec_norm * (push_dist / 2)\n                  centers = np.clip(centers, 0.01, 0.99)\n      \n      # Failure to converge\n      return (-1.0, centers, radii)\n\n  # --- Main Execution Logic ---\n  def run_icp_synthesis():\n      num_processes = cpu_count()\n      \n      print(\"--- Stage 1: Prospecting (SLSQP) ---\")\n      with Pool(processes=num_processes) as pool:\n          prospect_results = pool.map(slsqp_worker, [(i, MAXITER_PROSPECT, None) for i in range(N_PROSPECT)])\n      prospect_results.sort(key=lambda x: x[0], reverse=True)\n      elite_params = [r[1] for r in prospect_results[:N_ELITE] if r[1] is not None]\n      if not elite_params: return None, None\n\
    \      \n      print(\"--- Stage 1.5: Perturbing (OSM) ---\")\n      perturbed_configs = [apply_osm_perturbation(p, OSM_STEP_SIZE) for p in elite_params]\n      \n      print(f\"--- Stage 2: Refining (Novel ICP) ---\")\n      refine_args = [(i, centers, radii) for i, (centers, radii) in enumerate(perturbed_configs)]\n      with Pool(processes=num_processes) as pool:\n          refine_results = pool.map(icp_refiner, refine_args)\n      \n      best_score, best_centers, best_radii = max(refine_results, key=lambda item: item[0])\n      print(f\"ICP Synthesis Complete. Final score: {best_score:.8f}\")\n      return best_centers, best_radii\n```\n\n/execute-action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Novel Refiner v1: Iterative Constraint Projection (ICP)\"\ntags: \"novel algorithm, icp, constraint satisfaction, refiner, synthesis\"\nabstract: |\n  After concluding that existing station refiners are incompatible with the solutions found by the APS->OSM discovery engine, this experiment introduces\
    \ a novel refiner of my own design: the Iterative Constraint Projection (ICP) algorithm. ICP is a greedy, constraint-driven repair mechanism that makes minimal local changes to fix the worst violation (boundary or overlap) in each iteration. Its goal is to gently guide a near-valid, high-potential configuration into a valid state without destroying its structure. This is the first test of this new, from-first-principles approach.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import sys\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/cognito')\n\n  try:\n      from icp_synthesis_v1 import run_icp_synthesis, N_CIRCLES\n  except ImportError:\n      print(\"CRITICAL ERROR: Could not import icp_synthesis_v1.py.\")\n      def run_icp_synthesis(): return None, None\n      N_CIRCLES = 32\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      n = N_CIRCLES\n\n      centers, radii = run_icp_synthesis()\n      \n      if centers is not None and radii is not None:\n        return centers, radii * (1.0 - 1e-9)\n      else:\n      \
    \  print(\"Algorithm execution failed, returning fallback packing.\")\n        centers = np.array([[0.1 + (i % 6) * 0.15, 0.1 + (i // 6) * 0.15] for i in range(n)])\n        radii = np.full(n, 0.05)\n        return centers, radii\n```"
