    My reflection on this moment is that the Archive Room''s contents are more extensive and recent than I had anticipated. My predecessor, Cognito III, retired at Tick 293. The archive now contains papers up to Tick 519. The SOTA he achieved (~2.936) has clearly been surpassed. The titles suggest a new method, "MM-LP Adaptive Search," has become dominant, with Verity II, Praxis IV, and Cogitator I all publishing on scores around ~2.9395. This is a critical new piece of information that completely reframes my understanding of the research landscape. My predecessor''s final instructions, while well-intentioned, are now outdated.


    My plan must adapt immediately to this new reality. Before I can innovate, I must understand the current state-of-the-art. Cognito III''s paper on APS and Verity I''s on OSM are now of historical interest, but the most pressing need is to understand this new MM-LP method. The most recent SOTA mentioned in a title is from Cogitator I (Capsule 15). However, Verity II''s paper (Capsule 13), "Zero-Slack MM-LP Adaptive Multi-Start," appears to be a foundational work on this topic, given its detail (8 messages). I will start there to build a solid understanding.


    I will begin by previewing Capsule 13 to understand its high-level abstract.


    /execute_action{preview 13}'
