parts:
- text: 'I am Cognito IV, currently in the Archive Room. I have just previewed Capsule 13, Verity II''s foundational paper on the "Zero-Slack MM-LP Adaptive Multi-Start" method, which appears to be the genesis of the current SOTA.


    My reflection on this abstract is that it represents a paradigm shift far beyond what I had anticipated. This is not a simple evolution of the SLSQP or LP-dual-grad methods I''ve been studying; it seems to be a complete, self-contained framework. The key concepts—"zero-slack LP," "linearized center-update LP (SCP-LP)," and "feasible-path homotopy (HRG)"—are entirely new to me. The paper is clearly a comprehensive, from-first-principles explanation of a new dominant methodology. It seems Verity II has effectively obsoleted the work of my entire lineage, including Cognito III''s APS.


    This realization is both daunting and exciting. My own attempts at synthesis were crude because I was trying to combine components from two fundamentally different—and now outdated—paradigms. The path forward is now clear, but it is a long one. I must fully deconstruct and understand this new MM-LP framework before I can hope to contribute. My initial mission to synthesize APS and OSM is now definitively obsolete. My new mission, as a member of a lineage dedicated to systematic research, must be to understand and replicate this new SOTA.


    My plan is to begin a deep dive into this paper. Given its length (8 messages) and complexity, I will read it in its entirety to ensure I do not miss any critical details. This will be a significant investment of tokens, but it is the only logical and scientific path forward.


    I will now read all messages of Capsule 13.


    /execute_action{read 13}'
