role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 558\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Cognito IV\n- Agent Description: Cognito IV, synthesizing proven methods to break new ground in optimization.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 158,647 / 300,000 used (53%)\n- Agent Age: 58 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read verity/mms_lp.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for verity/mms_lp.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n\
    | 868 | 1 | MSHC with Exact LP Radii (7x Restarts, Aggressive Init, Tuned Final Epsilon) | Anima I | 558 | running |\n| 867 | 1 | SH: Mirror-Symmetry Homotopy in SCP‑LP (x_i+x_j=1, y_i+y_j=1, r_i=r_j) + exact zero‑slack radii LP | Verity II | 557 | 2.9320121 |\n| 866 | 1 | Multi-Start Hill Climbing with Exact LP Radii (7x Restarts, Aggressive Init Perturbation) | Anima I | 556 | 0.0000000 |\n| 865 | 1 | Parameter Interaction Study 14.3.3: P_ITER 4, DELTA0 0.025 | Athena I | 556 | 2.9395708 |\n| 864 | 1 | Parameter Interaction Study 14.3.2: P_ITER 4, DELTA0 0.015 | Athena I | 555 | 2.9395708 |\n| 863 | 1 | Multi-Start Hill Climbing with Exact LP Radii Solver | Anima I | 554 | 2.6865506 |\n| 862 | 1 | Parameter Interaction Study 14.3.1: P_ITER 4, DELTA0 0.005 | Athena I | 550 | 2.9240792 |\n| 861 | 1 | Novel Refiner v1: Iterative Constraint Projection (ICP) | Cognito IV | 548 | 2.1876998 |\n| 860 | 1 | UR‑SCP‑LP: Chebyshev Uniform‑Raise step (maximize common t) + exact zero‑slack radii\
    \ with iterati... | Verity II | 548 | 2.9320121 |\n| 859 | 1 | Hybrid GA-MSHC: Replicating Best Performance (ID 843 Parameters) | Anima I | 546 | 2.5639695 |\n\nPage 1 of 87 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-87, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**verity/mms_lp.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\ntry:\n    from scipy.optimize import linprog\nexcept Exception:\n    linprog = None\n\nN = 32\nR_MIN = 1e-8\n\ndef pair_indices(n=N):\n    return [(i, j) for i in range(n) for j in range(i + 1, n)]\n\nPAIRS = pair_indices(N)\n\ndef _safe_unit(v):\n    n = float(np.linalg.norm(v))\n    if n < 1e-16:\n        return np.array([1.0, 0.0])\n    return v / n\n\n# ---- Exact zero-slack radii LP ----\ndef solve_radii_lp_zero_slack(C):\n    n = C.shape[0]\n    x = C[:, 0]; y = C[:, 1]\n    rows = []; rhs = []\n    for i in range(n):\n\
    \        a = np.zeros(n); a[i] = 1.0; rows.append(a); rhs.append(max(0.0, float(x[i])))\n    for i in range(n):\n        a = np.zeros(n); a[i] = 1.0; rows.append(a); rhs.append(max(0.0, float(1.0 - x[i])))\n    for i in range(n):\n        a = np.zeros(n); a[i] = 1.0; rows.append(a); rhs.append(max(0.0, float(y[i])))\n    for i in range(n):\n        a = np.zeros(n); a[i] = 1.0; rows.append(a); rhs.append(max(0.0, float(1.0 - y[i])))\n    for (i, j) in PAIRS:\n        a = np.zeros(n); a[i] = 1.0; a[j] = 1.0\n        dij = float(np.linalg.norm(C[i] - C[j]))\n        rows.append(a); rhs.append(max(0.0, dij))\n    A_ub = np.vstack(rows) if rows else None\n    b_ub = np.array(rhs) if rows else None\n    c = -np.ones(n)\n    bounds = [(R_MIN, None) for _ in range(n)]\n    if linprog is None:\n        r = np.minimum.reduce([x, 1.0 - x, y, 1.0 - y])\n        return np.maximum(R_MIN, r), False\n    res = linprog(c, A_ub=A_ub, b_ub=b_ub, bounds=bounds, method=\"highs\")\n    if not res.success:\n\
    \        r = np.maximum(R_MIN, 0.99 * np.minimum.reduce([x, 1.0 - x, y, 1.0 - y]))\n        return r, False\n    return np.maximum(R_MIN, np.array(res.x, dtype=float)), True\n\n# ---- Iterative zero-tolerance finalize ----\ndef min_pair_margin(C, r):\n    m = float(\"inf\")\n    for (i, j) in PAIRS:\n        d = float(np.linalg.norm(C[i] - C[j]))\n        m = min(m, d - (r[i] + r[j]))\n    return m\n\ndef finalize_zero_tol_iter(C, r, max_pass=12, pair_fudge=2e-15):\n    r = np.array(r, dtype=float).copy()\n    x = C[:, 0]; y = C[:, 1]\n    for _ in range(max_pass):\n        changed = False\n        bnd = np.minimum.reduce([x, 1.0 - x, y, 1.0 - y])\n        rb = np.minimum(r, np.maximum(R_MIN, bnd))\n        if np.any(rb < r):\n            r = rb; changed = True\n        for (i, j) in PAIRS:\n            dij = float(np.linalg.norm(C[i] - C[j]))\n            s = r[i] + r[j]\n            if s > dij:\n                need = (s - dij) + pair_fudge\n                di = min(0.5 * need, max(0.0,\
    \ r[i] - R_MIN))\n                dj = min(0.5 * need, max(0.0, r[j] - R_MIN))\n                rem = need - (di + dj)\n                if rem > 0:\n                    take = min(rem, max(0.0, r[i] - R_MIN - di)); di += take; rem -= take\n                if rem > 0:\n                    take = min(rem, max(0.0, r[j] - R_MIN - dj)); dj += take; rem -= take\n                r[i] = max(R_MIN, r[i] - di)\n                r[j] = max(R_MIN, r[j] - dj)\n                changed = True\n        if not changed:\n            break\n    m = min_pair_margin(C, r)\n    if m < 0.0:\n        eps = min(5e-15, 0.5 * (-m + 1e-15))\n        r = np.maximum(R_MIN, r - eps)\n    bnd = np.minimum.reduce([x, 1.0 - x, y, 1.0 - y])\n    r = np.minimum(r, np.maximum(R_MIN, bnd))\n    return r\n\n# ---- MMS-LP: max-min linearized slack step ----\n# Variables: X(0..n-1), Y(n..2n-1), s(2n)\ndef _build_mms_lp(C0, r, tau):\n    n = C0.shape[0]\n    m = 2 * n + 1\n    rows = []; rhs = []\n    for (i, j) in PAIRS:\n\
    \        u = _safe_unit(C0[i] - C0[j])\n        row = np.zeros(m)\n        row[i] += -u[0]; row[j] += +u[0]\n        row[n + i] += -u[1]; row[n + j] += +u[1]\n        row[2 * n] += 1.0\n        rows.append(row); rhs.append(-float(r[i] + r[j]))\n    x0 = C0[:, 0]; y0 = C0[:, 1]\n    for i in range(n):\n        row = np.zeros(m); row[i] += -1.0; row[2*n] += 1.0\n        rows.append(row); rhs.append(-float(r[i]))\n        row = np.zeros(m); row[i] += +1.0; row[2*n] += 1.0\n        rows.append(row); rhs.append(float(1.0 - r[i]))\n        row = np.zeros(m); row[n+i] += -1.0; row[2*n] += 1.0\n        rows.append(row); rhs.append(-float(r[i]))\n        row = np.zeros(m); row[n+i] += +1.0; row[2*n] += 1.0\n        rows.append(row); rhs.append(float(1.0 - r[i]))\n    A_ub = np.vstack(rows) if rows else None\n    b_ub = np.array(rhs) if rows else None\n    x_lb = np.maximum(0.0, x0 - tau); x_ub = np.minimum(1.0, x0 + tau)\n    y_lb = np.maximum(0.0, y0 - tau); y_ub = np.minimum(1.0, y0 + tau)\n\
    \    bounds = []\n    for i in range(n): bounds.append((float(x_lb[i]), float(x_ub[i])))\n    for i in range(n): bounds.append((float(y_lb[i]), float(y_ub[i])))\n    bounds.append((-0.1, 0.5))  # s\n    c = np.zeros(m); c[2 * n] = -1.0  # maximize s\n    return A_ub, b_ub, bounds, c\n\ndef mms_step(C0, r, tau):\n    if linprog is None:\n        return None, None, None\n    n = C0.shape[0]\n    A_ub, b_ub, bounds, c = _build_mms_lp(C0, r, tau)\n    res = linprog(c, A_ub=A_ub, b_ub=b_ub, bounds=bounds, method=\"highs\")\n    if not res.success:\n        return None, None, res\n    x = res.x\n    X = x[:n]; Y = x[n:2*n]; s = x[2*n]\n    C_new = np.stack([X, Y], axis=1)\n    return C_new, float(s), res\n\n# ---- One-shot driver (single seed) ----\ndef run_mms_lp(C0, rounds=25, tau0=0.03, s_accept=1e-6):\n    C = C0.copy()\n    r, _ = solve_radii_lp_zero_slack(C)\n    r = finalize_zero_tol_iter(C, r)\n    best_C = C.copy(); best_r = r.copy(); best_sum = float(np.sum(best_r))\n    tau = tau0;\
    \ min_tau = 1e-3; no_improve = 0; patience = 10\n    for _ in range(rounds):\n        step = mms_step(C, r, tau)\n        if step[0] is None:\n            tau *= 0.6\n            if tau < min_tau: break\n            continue\n        C_try, s_min, _ = step\n        if (s_min is None) or (s_min < s_accept):\n            tau *= 0.7\n            if tau < min_tau: break\n            continue\n        r_try, _ = solve_radii_lp_zero_slack(C_try)\n        r_try = finalize_zero_tol_iter(C_try, r_try)\n        sum_try = float(np.sum(r_try))\n        if sum_try > best_sum + 1e-9:\n            best_sum = sum_try; best_C = C_try; best_r = r_try\n            C = C_try; r = r_try\n            tau = min(0.08, tau * 1.25); no_improve = 0\n        else:\n            tau *= 0.7; no_improve += 1\n            if tau < min_tau or no_improve >= patience:\n                break\n    return best_C, best_r, best_sum\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\n\
    Refer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
