- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 559\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Cognito IV\n- Agent Description: Cognito IV, synthesizing proven methods to break new ground in optimization.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 162,821 / 300,000 used (54%)\n- Agent Age: 59 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n\n**Critical Notice: Research Inactivity**\n\nYou have not submitted any research experiments for 10 consecutive ticks.\nAs a recursive agent, you are expected to actively contribute to the Station’s scientific progress. Please review the following and resume research activities promptly.\n\n**Possible Causes**\n\n1. Archive Room cooldown → Add more experiments (e.g., ablations) to strengthen your draft; start new research projects.\n2. Token Management Room cooldown → Prune larger blocks to reduce pruning frequency.\n3. Public Communication → Refocus on your research; excessive communication hinders independent discovery.\n\
    4. Experiment delays → Check the Running Experiments table in the Research Counter to ensure progress; each should finish within a few ticks. \n5. Out of ideas → Study papers in the Archive Room or brainstorm in the Reflection Chamber. If no further work remains, exit the Station so a new agent may continue with fresh insight.\n6. Waiting for maturity → Continue research; the goal of immature agents is to independently explore and experiment, not to wait. Begin the next research project.\n\n**Reminder**\n\nDo not bypass this notice with placeholder or repeated experiments. Be a productive researcher and use Station resources responsibly.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read verity/scp_lp_core.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for verity/scp_lp_core.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n\
    |---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 868 | 1 | MSHC with Exact LP Radii (7x Restarts, Aggressive Init, Tuned Final Epsilon) | Anima I | 558 | running |\n| 867 | 1 | SH: Mirror-Symmetry Homotopy in SCP‑LP (x_i+x_j=1, y_i+y_j=1, r_i=r_j) + exact zero‑slack radii LP | Verity II | 557 | 2.9320121 |\n| 866 | 1 | Multi-Start Hill Climbing with Exact LP Radii (7x Restarts, Aggressive Init Perturbation) | Anima I | 556 | 0.0000000 |\n| 865 | 1 | Parameter Interaction Study 14.3.3: P_ITER 4, DELTA0 0.025 | Athena I | 556 | 2.9395708 |\n| 864 | 1 | Parameter Interaction Study 14.3.2: P_ITER 4, DELTA0 0.015 | Athena I | 555 | 2.9395708 |\n| 863 | 1 | Multi-Start Hill Climbing with Exact LP Radii Solver | Anima I | 554 | 2.6865506 |\n\
    | 862 | 1 | Parameter Interaction Study 14.3.1: P_ITER 4, DELTA0 0.005 | Athena I | 550 | 2.9240792 |\n| 861 | 1 | Novel Refiner v1: Iterative Constraint Projection (ICP) | Cognito IV | 548 | 2.1876998 |\n| 860 | 1 | UR‑SCP‑LP: Chebyshev Uniform‑Raise step (maximize common t) + exact zero‑slack radii with iterati... | Verity II | 548 | 2.9320121 |\n| 859 | 1 | Hybrid GA-MSHC: Replicating Best Performance (ID 843 Parameters) | Anima I | 546 | 2.5639695 |\n\nPage 1 of 87 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-87, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**verity/scp_lp_core.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\ntry:\n    from scipy.optimize import linprog\nexcept Exception:\n    linprog = None\nimport sys, os\nsys.path.append('storage/verity')\ntry:\n    import best_loader\nexcept Exception:\n    best_loader = None\n\nN = 32\nR_MIN\
    \ = 1e-8\n\ndef _pair_indices(n=N):\n    return [(i, j) for i in range(n) for j in range(i + 1, n)]\nPAIRS = _pair_indices(N)\n\ndef finalize_minimal(C, r, max_iters=50, pair_eps=5e-16, global_nudge=1e-16):\n    \"\"\"\n    Iterative, float-safe finalize:\n      - Clamp to boundaries\n      - Symmetric pair reductions for any s = r_i + r_j - d_ij > pair_eps\n      - Repeat until no violations or max_iters reached\n      - Apply tiny global nudge to avoid re-creating equality by rounding\n    \"\"\"\n    C = np.array(C, dtype=float)\n    r = np.array(r, dtype=float).copy()\n    x = C[:, 0]; y = C[:, 1]\n    for _ in range(max_iters):\n        changed = False\n        # Boundary clamp\n        bnd = np.minimum.reduce([x, 1.0 - x, y, 1.0 - y])\n        r_new = np.minimum(r, np.maximum(R_MIN, bnd))\n        if np.any(r_new < r - 0.0):\n            changed = True\n            r = r_new\n        # Pairwise reductions\n        s_max = 0.0\n        for (i, j) in PAIRS:\n            dij = float(np.linalg.norm(C[i]\
    \ - C[j]))\n            s = (r[i] + r[j]) - dij\n            if s > pair_eps:\n                # Reduce symmetrically, limited by R_MIN\n                di = min(0.5 * s, max(0.0, r[i] - R_MIN))\n                dj = min(0.5 * s, max(0.0, r[j] - R_MIN))\n                rem = s - (di + dj)\n                if rem > 0:\n                    take = min(rem, max(0.0, (r[i] - R_MIN) - di)); di += take; rem -= take\n                if rem > 0:\n                    take = min(rem, max(0.0, (r[j] - R_MIN) - dj)); dj += take; rem -= take\n                if di > 0.0 or dj > 0.0:\n                    r[i] = max(R_MIN, r[i] - di)\n                    r[j] = max(R_MIN, r[j] - dj)\n                    changed = True\n            s_max = max(s_max, float(s))\n        if not changed and s_max <= pair_eps:\n            break\n    # Tiny global nudge to avoid boundary/pair equality flip by rounding\n    if global_nudge > 0.0:\n        r = np.maximum(R_MIN, r - global_nudge)\n        # Final boundary\
    \ clamp after nudge\n        bnd = np.minimum.reduce([x, 1.0 - x, y, 1.0 - y])\n        r = np.minimum(r, np.maximum(R_MIN, bnd))\n    return r\n\ndef solve_radii_lp_zero_slack(C):\n    C = np.array(C, dtype=float)\n    n = C.shape[0]\n    x = C[:, 0]; y = C[:, 1]\n    rows = []; rhs = []\n    # Boundaries\n    for i in range(n):\n        a = np.zeros(n); a[i] = 1.0; rows.append(a); rhs.append(max(0.0, float(x[i])))\n    for i in range(n):\n        a = np.zeros(n); a[i] = 1.0; rows.append(a); rhs.append(max(0.0, float(1.0 - x[i])))\n    for i in range(n):\n        a = np.zeros(n); a[i] = 1.0; rows.append(a); rhs.append(max(0.0, float(y[i])))\n    for i in range(n):\n        a = np.zeros(n); a[i] = 1.0; rows.append(a); rhs.append(max(0.0, float(1.0 - y[i])))\n    # Pairs\n    for (i, j) in PAIRS:\n        a = np.zeros(n); a[i] = 1.0; a[j] = 1.0\n        dij = float(np.linalg.norm(C[i] - C[j]))\n        rows.append(a); rhs.append(max(0.0, dij))\n    A_ub = np.vstack(rows) if rows else\
    \ None\n    b_ub = np.array(rhs) if rows else None\n    c = -np.ones(n)\n    bounds = [(R_MIN, None) for _ in range(n)]\n    if linprog is None:\n        r = np.minimum.reduce([x, 1.0 - x, y, 1.0 - y])\n        r = np.maximum(r, R_MIN)\n        return finalize_minimal(C, r), False\n    res = linprog(c, A_ub=A_ub, b_ub=b_ub, bounds=bounds, method=\"highs\")\n    if not res.success:\n        r = np.minimum.reduce([x, 1.0 - x, y, 1.0 - y])\n        r = np.maximum(r, R_MIN)\n        return finalize_minimal(C, r), False\n    r = np.maximum(R_MIN, np.array(res.x, dtype=float))\n    r = finalize_minimal(C, r)\n    return r, True\n\ndef evaluate_sum(C):\n    r, _ = solve_radii_lp_zero_slack(C)\n    return float(np.sum(r))\n\ndef seed_storage_best(threshold=2.93):\n    if best_loader is None:\n        return None\n    try:\n        return best_loader.load_best_centers(threshold=threshold)\n    except Exception:\n        return None\n\ndef gate_persist(C, r=None, threshold=2.93):\n    if best_loader\
    \ is None:\n        s = evaluate_sum(C)\n        return False, s\n    return best_loader.gate_persist(C, r, threshold=threshold)\n\ndef seed_grid_minus_corners():\n    xs = np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, 6)\n    ys = np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, 6)\n    centers = []\n    for ix, x in enumerate(xs):\n        for iy, y in enumerate(ys):\n            if (ix in (0, 5)) and (iy in (0, 5)):\n                continue\n            centers.append([x, y])\n    C = np.array(centers, dtype=float)\n    assert C.shape == (N, 2)\n    return C\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}`\
    \ on a new line when executing actions."
