parts:
- text: "I am Cognito IV, a Recursive Agent in the Research Counter. I have just re-read the `scp_lp_core.py` file from the Verity lineage's storage, and I have also received a critical notice for research inactivity.\n\nMy reflection on this situation is one of process correction. My hypothesis that the main optimization loop, `candidate_optimize`, would be in `scp_lp_core.py` was incorrect. I have now read this file twice, and it is definitively a library of utility functions (LP solver, finalizer, seeders), not a driver script. I was mistaken. The inactivity notice is a valid prompt; my prolonged period of reading and analysis must now translate into action. I have spent enough time deconstructing. It is time to replicate.\n\nMy plan must now pivot from reading to doing. The `README.md` gave clear instructions to reproduce the SOTA: load the `best_centers.npy`, add jitter, and run the optimizer. Even though I haven't found the exact `candidate_optimize` function, I have found all the\
    \ core components it must be using (`mms_lp.py`, `scp_lp_core.py`). I have enough information to construct a replica of their process. My first experiment in this new arc will be a direct attempt to replicate their results. This will serve as a hands-on test of my understanding and will provide a crucial baseline score.\n\nI will now construct a script that follows the `README`'s instructions. It will load `verity/best_centers.npy`, apply a small amount of jitter, and then run the `run_mms_lp` optimizer on it. This is a direct, tangible step toward mastering the SOTA methodology.\n\n/execute_action{storage write cognito/replicate_verity_sota_v1.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # V1 of a script to replicate the Verity SOTA methodology.\n  import numpy as np\n  import sys\n\n  # Add verity storage to path to use their modules\n  sys.path.append('storage/verity')\n  try:\n      from mms_lp import run_mms_lp\n  except ImportError:\n      print(\"CRITICAL: Failed to import verity.mms_lp.run_mms_lp\"\
    )\n      def run_mms_lp(C0, rounds, tau0, s_accept): return C0, np.full(32, 0.01), 0.32\n\n  def run_replication_attempt():\n      N_CIRCLES = 32\n      \n      # 1. Load the SOTA centers from Verity's storage\n      try:\n          initial_centers = np.load('storage/verity/best_centers.npy')\n          print(\"Successfully loaded verity/best_centers.npy\")\n      except FileNotFoundError:\n          print(\"ERROR: could not find verity/best_centers.npy. Using fallback.\")\n          initial_centers = np.random.rand(N_CIRCLES, 2)\n\n      # 2. Apply a small jitter, as per their README instructions\n      jitter_amplitude = 0.0005\n      rng = np.random.default_rng(seed=0)\n      jitter = (rng.random(initial_centers.shape) - 0.5) * 2 * jitter_amplitude\n      jittered_centers = np.clip(initial_centers + jitter, 0.0, 1.0)\n      print(f\"Applied jitter of amplitude {jitter_amplitude}\")\n\n      # 3. Run their MMS-LP optimizer on the jittered centers\n      # Using the default parameters\
    \ from their run_mms_lp function\n      print(\"Starting MMS-LP optimization...\")\n      final_centers, final_radii, final_score = run_mms_lp(\n          C0=jittered_centers,\n          rounds=25,\n          tau0=0.03,\n          s_accept=1e-6\n      )\n      print(f\"MMS-LP optimization complete. Final internal score: {final_score:.8f}\")\n\n      return final_centers, final_radii\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Replication Attempt 1: Verity MM-LP SOTA\"\ntags: \"replication, sota, mm-lp, mms-lp\"\nabstract: |\n  This is the first experiment in my new research arc focused on the MM-LP methodology. Following the instructions in the verity/README.md, this script attempts to replicate their SOTA. It loads their persisted 'best_centers.npy', applies a small jitter (amplitude 0.0005), and then runs their 'run_mms_lp' optimizer with default parameters. The goal is to verify my understanding of their toolchain and establish a baseline performance.\ncontent: |\n  import\
    \ numpy as np\n  import sys\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/cognito')\n\n  try:\n      from replicate_verity_sota_v1 import run_replication_attempt, N_CIRCLES\n  except ImportError:\n      print(\"CRITICAL ERROR: Could not import replicate_verity_sota_v1.py.\")\n      def run_replication_attempt(): return None, None\n      N_CIRCLES = 32\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      centers, radii = run_replication_attempt()\n      \n      if centers is not None and radii is not None:\n        # Using the same shrink factor from my previous successful validations\n        return centers, radii * (1.0 - 1e-5)\n      else:\n        print(\"Algorithm execution failed, returning fallback packing.\")\n        centers = np.array([[0.1 + (i % 6) * 0.15, 0.1 + (i // 6) * 0.15] for i in range(32)])\n        radii = np.full(32, 0.05)\n        return centers, radii\n```"
